Reference renders (used by build123d/tests/test_openconnect.py):
            These files need a newer BOSL2 than this repo's pin (456fcd8's
            std.scad does not include structs.scad, so every struct_val is
            undef and the render fails), so they were rendered ONCE outside
            the repo toolchain and committed. CI does not render them.

  openscad: 2025.06.12.ai25773 (the ci.yml pin)
  BOSL2:    https://github.com/BelfrySCAD/BOSL2 commit
            b86a7584db6d324eb856c2d19d041f94435e6c32 (HEAD on 2026-10-01 UTC,
            BOSL_VERSION 2.0.764), checked out at $BOSL2_PARENT/BOSL2
  Commands, run from assets/openConnect/:

    OPENSCADPATH=$BOSL2_PARENT openscad --export-format=binstl \
      -D plate_horizontal_size=28 -D plate_vertical_size=28 \
      -o mesh/openconnect_plate_one_slot.stl openconnect_plate.scad

    OPENSCADPATH=$BOSL2_PARENT openscad --export-format=binstl \
      -o mesh/openconnect_head.stl mesh/openconnect_head.scad

  The plate overrides make one 28 x 28 mm tile (the shipped default is
  84 x 56 = six slots). Every other setting is the shipped default:
  plate_size_unit "mm", plate_extra_thickness 0.5, slot_type "slot",
  slot_position "All" (= the one tile), slot_lock_distribution "Corners"
  (the one tile is a corner, so it has the left lock), slot_entryramp_flip
  false, clearances 0.1 / 0.1, slot_edge_feature_widen "Both". Result:
  28 x 28 x 3.2 mm, one slot 2.7 mm deep, watertight.

  sha256 of the committed renders:
    e6244038bdd2e46ba6db5e844e1aeb4868e4188ec3a59a2be45f6f9762578171  mesh/openconnect_plate_one_slot.stl
    b5a12a5024284c2a48faf87a54be4f58d9e9fda682d6ab1b85013c82c92757bb  mesh/openconnect_head.stl

  Re-running a command gives the same triangles in a different facet order,
  so the bytes (and sha256) change while the geometry does not. The hashes
  pin the committed files; the tests compare geometry.

These are reference assets only: not on OPENSCADPATH, not included by any
model, not a build dependency. See build123d/docs/openconnect-library.md.
